URGENT RULES
1. User agent strings must be sourced from user-agent.config.js and never hardcoded in provider implementations
2. Chrome version in user-agent.config.js must be updated monthly to maintain compatibility
3. All errors must be logged using electron-log with appropriate severity levels
4. Web security and context isolation must be enabled for all webviews

PROVIDER RULES
1. All provider classes must extend BaseProvider
2. All abstract methods in BaseProvider must be implemented by child classes
3. Provider files must be named with the pattern <provider-name>.provider.js
4. Provider initialization must handle user agent configuration correctly
5. Provider-specific user agents must be registered in getUserAgentForProvider

PROFILE MANAGEMENT RULES
1. Profile names must follow the pattern <provider>:<profile-name>
2. Profile data must be isolated using Electron session partitioning
3. Default profiles must be preserved during bulk operations
4. Profile options must be properly merged with defaults

CODE ORGANIZATION RULES
1. Service modules → src/services/
2. Provider implementations → src/providers/
3. Configuration files → src/config/
4. Utility functions → src/utils/

PERFORMANCE RULES
1. Heavy operations must not block the main thread
2. Event listeners must be properly cleaned up
3. Memory usage must be monitored for leaks

DEPENDENCY RULES
1. Electron version must be kept current with security updates
2. Dependencies must specify exact versions
3. Unused dependencies must be removed